Subject: [PATCH 1/1] config: turn MarkStoreEscaping off so the PYE Store rule runs

WHAT THIS CHANGES
-----------------
One boolean, in one file: config/StoreEscape.MarkStoreEscaping, true -> false.

WHY
---
With MarkStoreEscaping = true (the value in the upstream checkout),
handlers/JAssignStmt/StoreStmt.java:37 short-circuits every field store:

    if (StoreEscape.MarkStoreEscaping) {
        if (rhs instanceof Local) { ptg.cascadeEscape((Local)rhs, summary); return; }
    }

That `return` is taken BEFORE storeStmt() is reached, so for every `a.f = b`:

  * b, and everything reachable from b, is set to Escape
    (cascadeEscape -> recursiveCascadeEscape -> EscapeStatus.setEscape());
  * no PTG field edge is built - STRONG_makeField / WEAK_makeField never run,
    so the `Fields:` map in every .info file stays empty;
  * no PYE Store-rule conditional value is created - propagateES never runs;
  * b's existing conditional values are DISCARDED, because setEscape() calls
    purgeAndEscape(), which replaces the whole status set with {Escape}.

The net effect is that the Store rule described in Clustering-Design 1.2 - the
first of the three places dependency edges are said to be created - is dead code
in the shipped configuration. The containment edges this project set out to draw
do not exist while the flag is true.

Corroboration, from output already checked in to the upstream repo. stava/tests/test1
is `A.n=B; B.n=C; C.n=D; D.n=B`, four `new Node()` at BCI 0/8/16/24. In
stava/out/test1/Main.info:

    Fields:{}
    {<internal,24>=[Escape], <internal,8>=[Escape],
     <internal,0>=[NoEscape], <internal,16>=[Escape]}

A is the only object that never appears as a store RHS, and the only NoEscape.
Nothing in test1 escapes in reality.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE
-----------------------
Nothing else. ReduceParamDependence and MarkParamReturnEscaping keep their
upstream values (true and false). No handler, no resolver, no output format.
Objects that escape for a real reason - store to a static field, escape by
return, store into a field of a parameter, argument to an unavailable callee -
still escape, via their own rules. This flag governs only the blanket
"any field store escapes" over-approximation.

HOW IT IS APPLIED
-----------------
NEVER to stava/. The Makefile copies stava/src to heapviz/build/stava-src-pye/
and applies this patch to the copy:

    cp -r ../stava/src build/stava-src-pye
    (cd build/stava-src-pye/.. && patch -p1 -d stava-src-pye/.. < patches/0001-store-escape-off.patch)

The unpatched configuration is built from stava/src directly, compiled to a
separate output directory, so both configurations can be run over the same
corpus in the same session without either touching the reference checkout.

Figures produced from the patched build are captioned `MarkStoreEscaping=false
(patched)`; figures from the unpatched build are captioned
`MarkStoreEscaping=true (upstream default)`. No figure is published without one
of those two labels.

--- a/src/config/StoreEscape.java
+++ b/src/config/StoreEscape.java
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 package config;

 public class StoreEscape {
-    public static boolean MarkStoreEscaping = true;
+    public static boolean MarkStoreEscaping = false;
     public static boolean ReduceParamDependence = true;
     public static boolean MarkParamReturnEscaping = false;
 }
